rritation  rising in my souls as i  keep hearing the references  to jim crow i asked myself how many  americans  understand what jim crow  was  don't lecture me  about jim crow  i know this is not 1965.  that's what makes me so outraged  it's 2022  and they're blatantly removing more  polling places  from the counties where black and  latinos  are overrepresented members of the  congressional black caucus took a  last-minute stand outside the senate but  walked away knowing the voting rights  law was set to fail  joe manchin that pivotal senator from  west virginia said yesterday he's open  to changing the electoral college count  act the law by which congress counts the  electoral votes after a presidential  election that was the process  interrupted by the capital attack  january 6th but the outlook for that is  cloudy democrats have been emphatic they  want much bigger change gail  right cloudy normally never a good thing  thank you very much scott
 

